WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:06.799
Don't you also hate it when you just want

2
00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:09.500
to go from A to B, but the bike lane just

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.199
ends in the middle?

4
00:00:11.439 --> 00:00:13.500
Many people want to bike, but cities

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.140
don't build the

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.839
infrastructure that protects them

7
00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:16.600
from cars.

8
00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:20.039
Cities need to build bike networks of

9
00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:21.480
protected infrastructure

10
00:00:22.079 --> 00:00:24.539
that is well connected, direct

11
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.199
and spans the whole city

12
00:00:26.219 --> 00:00:27.379
like here in Copenhagen.

13
00:00:28.399 --> 00:00:29.679
But most cities don't.

14
00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:31.640
Like this one.

15
00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:35.740
This is a political issue, but it's also

16
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.240
a technical issue and

17
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.219
it's a lack of vision.

18
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.880
Since 2019 we have pioneered

19
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.820
a science of bicycle networks.

20
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.539
We have developed many computational

21
00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:48.159
approaches to grow or to

22
00:00:48.159 --> 00:00:50.560
fix bike networks and now we

23
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.840
are turning these tools into BikeNetKit,

24
00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.000
a usable software for

25
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.979
urban planners or for

26
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.799
citizens to create a compelling vision

27
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.560
for urban cycling in their city.

28
00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:04.420
And it's also free and open source.

29
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.200
Here you can see one of our tools in

30
00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:09.519
action, growing and

31
00:01:09.519 --> 00:01:11.739
fixing the bike network in this

32
00:01:11.739 --> 00:01:14.579
particular city, but it works for any

33
00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:16.000
city, including yours.

34
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.439
If you like this, join our efforts.

35
00:01:20.739 --> 00:01:23.500
Run BikeNetKit yourself and create and

36
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.480
share your own vision of your city.

37
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.379
Show that to your local politicians and

38
00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.760
urban planners and help

39
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.180
us develop BikeNetKit and

40
00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:31.900
spread the word.

41
00:01:32.819 --> 00:01:34.299
Go to bikenetkit.org

42
00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:35.319
for more information.

43
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.439
Thanks and enjoy the ride.
